{"id":"0d5fef79e71e464f","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-elliptic-operator.md","title":"Elliptic Operator","display":"df-elliptic-operator — Elliptic Operator","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-elliptic-operator","aliases":["58-df-elliptic-operator","Elliptic Operator","Ellipticity"],"display":"df-elliptic-operator — Elliptic Operator","depends_on":["[[../batch06/58-df-differential-operator.md]]","[[../batch05/58-df-principal-symbol.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-elliptic-operator"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-elliptic-operator</span><span>Elliptic Operator</span><span>Ellipticity</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-elliptic-operator — Elliptic Operator"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"76305a7e4d824323\" href=\"?note=76305a7e4d824323\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-differential-operator.md\">../batch06/58-df-differential-operator.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"248fe87a7170ad10\" href=\"?note=248fe87a7170ad10\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-principal-symbol.md\">../batch05/58-df-principal-symbol.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m\\in\\omega\">\\(m\\in\\omega\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\)</span> open</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P:C^\\infty(\\Omega)\\to C^\\infty(\\Omega)\">\\(P:C^\\infty(\\Omega)\\to C^\\infty(\\Omega)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma:\\Omega\\times\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb C\">\\(\\sigma:\\Omega\\times\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb C\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PrincipalSymbol}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PrincipalSymbol}_S\\)</span> (principal-symbol predicate from dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Elliptic}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Elliptic}_S\\)</span> (elliptic-operator predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}elliptic-operator} \\vdash \\mathrm{Elliptic}_S(P,\\sigma,\\Omega,n,m)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{PrincipalSymbol}_S(\\sigma,P,\\Omega,n,m)\\land\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\\forall\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\bigl(\\sigma(x,\\xi)\\neq0\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}elliptic-operator} \\vdash \\mathrm{Elliptic}_S(P,\\sigma,\\Omega,n,m)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{PrincipalSymbol}_S(\\sigma,P,\\Omega,n,m)\\land\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\\forall\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\bigl(\\sigma(x,\\xi)\\neq0\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom follows the scalar differential-operator convention supplied by the dependencies. For operators between vector bundles, nonvanishing is replaced by invertibility of the bundle-valued principal symbol.</li>\n<li>Compact resolvent: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(P + \\lambda)^{-1}\">\\((P + \\lambda)^{-1}\\)</span> compact for some <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span></li>\n<li>Self-adjoint elliptic: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"-i\\nabla\">\\(-i\\nabla\\)</span> on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^2\">\\(L^2\\)</span></li>\n<li>Elliptic regularity: solutions are smooth</li>\n<li>Atiyah-Singer index: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ind}(P) = \\dim\\ker P - \\dim\\mathrm{coker}P\">\\(\\mathrm{ind}(P) = \\dim\\ker P - \\dim\\mathrm{coker}P\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Gilkey, Invariance Theory</li>\n<li>Lawson and Michelsohn, Spin Geometry</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch06/58-df-differential-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"76305a7e4d824323","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-differential-operator.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-principal-symbol.md","status":"resolved","id":"248fe87a7170ad10","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-principal-symbol.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"m\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"P:C^\\infty(\\Omega)\\to C^\\infty(\\Omega)","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma:\\Omega\\times\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb C","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PrincipalSymbol}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Elliptic}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}elliptic-operator} \\vdash \\mathrm{Elliptic}_S(P,\\sigma,\\Omega,n,m)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{PrincipalSymbol}_S(\\sigma,P,\\Omega,n,m)\\land\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\\forall\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^n\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\bigl(\\sigma(x,\\xi)\\neq0\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"(P + \\lambda)^{-1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda","display":false},{"tex":"-i\\nabla","display":false},{"tex":"L^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ind}(P) = \\dim\\ker P - \\dim\\mathrm{coker}P","display":false}],"bytes":1521,"backlinks":[{"id":"8b69e359479982ba","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-476","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-elliptic-operator.md|58-df-elliptic-operator]]（batch11）"}],"outgoing":["76305a7e4d824323","248fe87a7170ad10"]}